---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Publications">
  <p class="mono-eyebrow mb-1"><span class="text-accent-blue">$</span> echo "kudos to my co-authors"</p>
  <h1 class="glitch is-intro mb-8 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-brand-text" data-text="Publications">Publications</h1>

  <!-- ====== 2026 ====== -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="mb-5 inline-block rounded-md bg-band-fn-pure px-3 py-1 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-white">2026</h2>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      <article class="border-b border-brand-border pb-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">"From Rocq to Metal: A Pipeline for Formally Verified Microcontroller Firmware"</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">V. Bergeron, K. Gorna</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">arXiv preprint arXiv:2606.02651</p>
        <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2606.02651" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mt-2 inline-block text-sm text-band-fn-pure underline underline-offset-2">Read paper &rarr;</a>
      </article>

      <article class="border-b border-brand-border pb-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">"Concolic Execution Optimized for Go Binaries using Ghidra's P-Code"</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">K. Gorna, N. Iooss, Y. Seurin, R. Khatoun</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">Software Engineering and Management: Theory and Applications, Volume 18, pp. 161–176</p>
        <a href="https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-032-06658-9_10" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mt-2 inline-block text-sm text-band-fn-pure underline underline-offset-2">Read paper &rarr;</a>
      </article>

      <article class="border-b border-brand-border pb-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">"From TinyGo to gc Compiler: Extending Zorya's Concolic Framework to Real-World Go Binaries"</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">K. Gorna, N. Iooss, Y. Seurin, R. Khatoun, K. Makan</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">30th ACM International Conference on Evaluation and Assessment in Software Engineering (EASE 2026)</p>
        <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.03492" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mt-2 inline-block text-sm text-band-fn-pure underline underline-offset-2">Read paper &rarr;</a>
      </article>

      <article class="border-b border-brand-border pb-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">"Zorya: Automated Concolic Execution of Single-Threaded Go Binaries"</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">K. Gorna, N. Iooss, Y. Seurin, R. Khatoun</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">41st ACM/SIGAPP Symposium on Applied Computing (SAC 2026), pp. 2037–2044</p>
        <a href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3748522.3779940" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mt-2 inline-block text-sm text-band-fn-pure underline underline-offset-2">Read paper &rarr;</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ====== 2025 ====== -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="mb-5 inline-block rounded-md bg-band-fn-pure px-3 py-1 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-white">2025</h2>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      <article class="border-b border-brand-border pb-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">"Exposing Go's Hidden Bugs: A Novel Concolic Framework"</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">K. Gorna, N. Iooss, Y. Seurin, R. Khatoun</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">23rd IEEE/ACIS International Conference on Software Engineering, Management and Applications (SERA 2025)</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-brand-body">The widespread adoption of the Go programming language in infrastructure backends and blockchain projects has heightened the need for improved security measures. In this work, we present Zorya, a novel methodology leveraging concrete and symbolic (concolic) execution to evaluate Go programs comprehensively. Our solution employs Ghidra's PCode as an intermediate representation (IR). This implementation detects runtime panics in the TinyGo compiler and supports both generic and custom invariants.</p>
        <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.20183" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mt-2 inline-block text-sm text-band-fn-pure underline underline-offset-2">Read paper &rarr;</a>
      </article>

      <article class="border-b border-brand-border pb-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">"La Menace dans le Champ des Cryptoactifs"</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">Les Annales des Mines, revue Enjeux Numériques, N°32 Décembre 2025</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-brand-body">Contribution au numéro spécial de la revue Enjeux Numériques consacré aux défis de cybersécurité d'aujourd'hui et des cinq prochaines années, à l'échelle nationale et européenne. Contribution portant sur "La menace dans le champ des cryptoactifs", avec pour objectif d'éduquer et expliquer les différents aspects du blockchain et du Web3 à travers le prisme de la cybersécurité.</p>
        <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="https://annales-des-mines.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/EN-2025-12-Numero-avec-couverture-pour-internet.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sm text-band-fn-pure underline underline-offset-2">Full issue (PDF) &rarr;</a>
          <a href="https://annales-des-mines.org/2025-12_sommaire_enjeux-numeriques-n32_cybersecurite-sommes-nous-prets/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sm text-band-fn-pure underline underline-offset-2">Table of contents &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <img src="/images/1764583381550.jpeg" alt="Les Annales des Mines – Enjeux Numériques N°32" class="mt-3 max-w-sm rounded-md border border-brand-border" loading="lazy" />
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ====== 2022 ====== -->
  <section class="mb-10">
    <h2 class="mb-5 inline-block rounded-md bg-band-fn-pure px-3 py-1 text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-white">2022</h2>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      <article class="border-b border-brand-border pb-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-brand-text">Cybersecurity for Blockchains and Cryptos 2022</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-brand-muted">KPMG / Blockchain Partner – June 2022</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-brand-body">
          <a href="https://bit.ly/3NxMOyk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-medium text-band-fn-pure underline underline-offset-2">Download the study</a>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-medium text-brand-body">Media articles related to the study:</p>
        <ul class="ml-5 mt-1 list-disc space-y-1 text-sm text-brand-body">
          <li><a href="https://www.bfmtv.com/crypto/blockchain/cybersecurite-on-manque-cruellement-d-experts-pour-contrer-les-hacks-dans-les-cryptos_AV-202206150219.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-band-fn-pure underline underline-offset-2">BFM Business</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://cryptoast.fr/kpmg-pointe-efforts-mener-securite-web3/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-band-fn-pure underline underline-offset-2">Cryptoast</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://geeky.news/cybersecurity-we-are-sorely-lacking-in-experts-to-counter-crypto-hacks/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-band-fn-pure underline underline-offset-2">Geeky.news</a></li>
        </ul>
        <img src="/images/cyber-study.png" alt="Cybersecurity for Blockchains and Cryptos 2022 study" class="mt-3 max-w-md rounded-md border border-brand-border" loading="lazy" />
